# Phase 9 checks for the admin's customer directory (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above a block).
# Start the API first (npm run dev:api) and load the sample data (npm run seed:api). A contact correction
# made here stays in the database: run npm run seed:api again afterwards.
#
# Every request needs an admin token: get one with the sign-in requests at the top of catalog.http and
# paste it into @adminToken below. A customer's token gets 403 FORBIDDEN, no token 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
# Errors come back as { code, message, meta }.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api
@adminToken = paste-an-admin-token
@customerToken = paste-a-customer-token
@customer = cus-009

### Every customer with their summary (reservationCount, upcomingCount, completedCount, balance, totalSpend), by name
GET {{api}}/admin/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### One customer's summary and their reservations (newest event date first, each with its money figures)
### An unknown id, or one spelled differently (CUS-009): 404 "Customer not found."
GET {{api}}/admin/customers/{{customer}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Correct the email and mobile number -> the customer's summary. Saved as "new.address@example.com" and "09175551234".
### A bad email or mobile: 400 INVALID with meta.field; another customer's email: 409 EMAIL_TAKEN
PATCH {{api}}/admin/customers/{{customer}}/contact
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  New.Address@Example.COM ", "mobile": "0917-555 1234" }

### A customer's token on the directory: 403 FORBIDDEN (personal information, admin only)
GET {{api}}/admin/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
